Local patch to ZMK, applied by build.sh before every build.
(west update resets the zmk checkout, so build.sh re-applies this each time.)

Why: zmk,kscan-gpio-direct configures its pins with GPIO_INT_LEVEL_ACTIVE. The
nRF GPIO driver only routes a pin through the DETECT/PORT-sense mechanism - the
one that can wake the chip from System OFF - for EDGE interrupts on pins listed
in sense-edge-mask. A level interrupt takes a GPIOTE channel instead, which
cannot wake from System OFF. Behaviour while running is unchanged: the driver
polls the pins to detect a release, so edge interrupts scan the same way.

Requires, in config/boards/shields/swifty/swifty.dtsi:
  - wakeup-source; on kscan0            (ZMK then leaves it configured on suspend)
  - sense-edge-mask on &gpio0/&gpio1    (arm the sense lines for the key pins)

Refresh with:  git -C zmk diff > zmk.patch
diff --git a/app/module/drivers/kscan/kscan_gpio_direct.c b/app/module/drivers/kscan/kscan_gpio_direct.c
index 45fc8634..25f580ee 100644
--- a/app/module/drivers/kscan/kscan_gpio_direct.c
+++ b/app/module/drivers/kscan/kscan_gpio_direct.c
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ static int kscan_direct_interrupt_configure(const struct device *dev, const gpio
 
 #if USE_INTERRUPTS
 static int kscan_direct_interrupt_enable(const struct device *dev) {
-    return kscan_direct_interrupt_configure(dev, GPIO_INT_LEVEL_ACTIVE);
+    return kscan_direct_interrupt_configure(dev, GPIO_INT_EDGE_BOTH);
 }
 #endif
 
